DOCKER_REGISTRY=christopherguzman
NAMESPACE=website
API_URL=http://localhost:8000
TAVILY_API_KEY=your_tavily_api_key
SCRAPER_URL=https://scraper.iguzman.com.mx
SCRAPER_API_KEY=your_scraper_api_key

# DEVELOPMENT ONLY - which customer site `pnpm dev` is working on, by slug (see
# sites/registry.ts): piccolopizzas, supertortaselchino, bdrone, ...
# Ignored entirely in production, where the tenant comes from the request host.
#
# Leave it EMPTY and the tenant is unresolved on localhost (which matches no
# System.host): the site renders the `_default` fallback and every auth route
# refuses with a 503 telling you to set this. That refusal is deliberate - it
# used to substitute System 1 instead, which signed you in as that customer's
# admin and quietly filed every menu item, category and product you saved in the
# CMS onto them. Set it before signing in.
DEV_SITE=

# Note: LLM keys (GROQ_API_KEY / OPENROUTER_API_KEY) now live in website-api - see
# its env.example. Keep this note below every key: `pnpm secrets` treats any comment
# as the section heading for the keys that follow it.
